@startuml roles_knowledge_matrix

title Knowledge Domains by Role

!procedure $role($name, $vendor, $generic, $appspec, $analysis, $domain)
| $name | $vendor | $generic | $appspec | $analysis | $domain |
!endprocedure

skinparam backgroundColor white

package "Knowledge Matrix" {
    component table [
        | | **Vendor Format** | **Generic Semantics** | **App Specification** | **Analysis Methods** | **Domain Knowledge** |
        | **Data Converter** | ✓ Required | ✓ Creates | ✗ Not needed | ✗ Not needed | Minimal |
        | **Metadata Writer** | ✗ Not needed* | ✓ Uses (if present) | ✓ Required | ✗ Not needed | Minimal |
        | **Secondary Data Producer** | ✗ Not needed | ✗ Not needed | ✓ Required | ✓ Required | Moderate |
        | **Application Developer** | ✗ Not needed | ✗ Not used | ✓ Defines | ✗ Not needed | Moderate |
        | **End User / Researcher** | ✗ Not needed | ✗ Not needed | ✗ Not needed | ✗ Not needed | ✓ High |
    ]
}

note bottom of table
  * Metadata Writer doesn't need vendor format knowledge
    IF generic_semantics exists

  ✓ = Knowledge required for this role
  ✗ = Knowledge NOT needed for this role
end note

@enduml
